00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:57.060
type of accountability you're talking about.
Speaker 5: So I'm more boring. I'm sorry. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:03.660
more on the, you know, the economical side I&nbsp;
definitely like or, you know, far left on people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.229
should be allowed to do what they do.
Speaker 1: And yeah, no, I wasn't.&nbsp;

00:06:06.229 --> 00:06:08.460
Speaker 5: Suggesting they were.
Speaker 1: Taking any particular position on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.820
abortion. No, I don't I don't think I'm there. I&nbsp;
don't think I'm there on accountability. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:17.880
a lot of times there's this instinct sometimes&nbsp;
and I say this not to criticize you, but because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:23.820
a lot of people do this, there's this instinct to&nbsp;
find sort of like the grand thing that explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.860
